 "trace": {
  "model.nose.profile": "ptr (220018, side-on), the nose's silhouette against the background, read on 25 px grids at 1.75x: x = (1303 - u)/280, y = (1555 - v)/280 (bumper front u 1303, rail v 1555, 280 px/m from rail-to-roof 3.75 m and the 222 px wheel = 0.79 m). The diagram draws the upper nose 0.3-0.5 m longer (at 2.4 m up: diagram 0.87, photo 0.55; at 3.4 m: 1.90 vs 1.42): the photo wins.",
  "model.cab.doors[0]": "Cab door 2.78-3.42 m from the tip (centre 3.10, 0.64 wide): ptr (side-on, 280 px/m) and ped (camera solved on door 1 and three windows, held-out 3.8/7.9 cm; sidexy back-projection 2.79-3.42) agree within 1 cm. The diagram draws it at 3.54-4.17: its cab is drawn about 0.75 m long.",
  "model.nose.glazing": "ptr: the teardrop cab side window, outline read on the 1.75x grid (u 626-860, v 681-856): 1.58-2.42 m back, 2.50-3.12 m up.",
  "model.heights": "ptm1 (side-on, 196 px/m from rail-to-roof 3.75): body bottom 0.94, glass 2.02-2.90, orange cantrail line 3.33-3.43 (taken 3.36); roof 3.75 published.",
  "model.cab.windows": "dia row 140, glass runs (42,42,42) at 74.8 px/m from the tip (col 33).",
  "model.cab.doors[1-2]": "dia row 140, door colour runs (195,0,69): 6.80-7.89, 21.50-22.58.",
  "model.cab.bogies": "Front bogie: ptr shows its leading axle 2.83 m behind the tip, under the cab door (the diagram draws it 1 m ahead of the door: wrong in the cab region, as the door is); wheelbase 2.25 as published (the 222's photo pe0 reads 2.30 for the same Bombardier bogie; the diagram's 2.54 is not borne out): centre 2.83 + 1.125 = 3.96. Rear bogie 20.72 from the diagram (its saloon is borne out by the ped camera).",
  "model.next": "dia car 2 from its body start (col 1854): doors 1.03-2.11, 19.79-20.87; windows as listed; body 1854-3492 = 21.90 m; axles 1975/2165, 3181/3371.",
  "model.form": "setback and tumblehome provisional (not yet measured): to be fitted on the three-quarter photos (ped, prd).",
  "model.form.front": "The old scheme's face, as the 221's (classes/221 trace model.form.front): yellow round the screen to the roof. The 2026 red scheme's face (black above the screen) is kept as alternates.XC-red.",
  "model.form.setback": "Provisional, read from ptr/ped/ptg (±0.15 m): the nose's flank stands 0.3-0.35 m behind the centre-line profile at the bumper and lamps, 0.7-0.75 m at the windscreen, closing to 0 at the roof. To refine on a camera with off-plane picks.",
  "liveries.XC": "CrossCountry as refreshed from Feb 2026 (ped, ptmr, prd, ptg, ptm1: 2026 photos; the maroon and silver scheme is still on unrefurbished units, pso 2026-06: which is the default is open). Colours from samples.json (ptm1 overcast, balanced on the canopy white): red #B90B20, teal doors #76D2E5, car 2 dark grey #3B3F43, cream cantrail line #FAD091, roof #414A58; yellow #FFBA2F (pkn). The cream X on the cab car side: rear arm from the cantrail at 3.51-5.11 m to the solebar at 3.30-5.02 with the red '<' notch at 4.0/2.14, front arm from the cab door's front (2.4-2.74 at 2.1-2.4 m) down to the solebar at 1.1-1.9, back-projected through the ped camera (±0.2 m on the nose's curve).",
  "liveries.XC.branding": "The 'crosscountry X' wordmark in cream on the lower bodyside. Cab car: ped (220023, 2026), its corners back-projected through the ped camera (held-out 3.8/7.9 cm): 8.81-11.76 m, 1.12-1.69 m (the X's tips). Car 2: ptm1 (side-on, 2026), against its door 1 (1.03-2.11): 2.85-5.64 m, 1.14-1.58. Width given: the vinyl is squatter than logos/XC.svg (5.2-6.3 against 5.8). Colour the cream of the X stripes.",
  "model.form.front.panelFoot": "The yellow's foot at the sides 1.40 (photo 1.32): at 1.32 its corners sat in the crease where the bumper's top lip meets the face and the decal clearance check read 0.15 mm off the body.",
  "model.form.front.couplerRecess": "The coupler recess between the two red bumper blocks (ptg levelled, 466 px/m: ±0.55 m, from the bottom to the yellow's notch at 1.55), black: the render showed a solid red nose there.",
  "liveries.XC.choice": "The livery rule (2026-10-06, FLEET.md): the livery most units carry today, newer on a near tie. Commons photos dated 2026 (fetched 2026-10-06), each unit's latest: refreshed red 220007, 021, 023, 025, 027, 028, 033 (7); maroon and silver 220002, 004, 010, 012, 014, 015, 017, 020, 022, 031, 034 (11), the latest of them August 2026; refurbishment began February 2026 (Wikipedia). So the maroon and silver scheme, as on the 221 (classes/221/spec.json liveries.XC, the same scheme on the same body, with its flank mark); the red refresh is kept as liveries.XC-red (with its face, alternates.XC-red) for when it becomes the majority.",
  "model.form.front.pockets": "The coupler opening between the bumper blocks cut 0.3 m back (a void with the coupler in it), not painted black."
 },
